WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.130
- [Instructor] In this video,

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.810
we're going to try to
compute 6742 times 23.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.980
So like always, pause this video and try

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:08.473
to compute it for yourself.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.860
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.830
And I'm going to do it
using what's often known

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.040
as the standard algorithm.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:20.370
Algorithm is just a fancy
word for a series of steps,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.520
a process for doing something.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:26.670
So we have 6742 times 23.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.350
And so I'm gonna write the 23

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.850
in the same place values.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.360
So that's two 10s, so I'm gonna write it

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.100
under the four 10s over there.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.310
And then three ones.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.990
I'll write it under the two ones.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.020
And it's important to realize

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.020
this isn't the only way
to multiply numbers.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.970
In fact, we've studied
other methods for doing it

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.960
in other videos.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.130
And it's important to realize
what's really going on

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.770
and how these different methods are all,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.380
on some level, doing the same thing,

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.790
maybe just writing them different

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.850
or doing them in different orders.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.460
So the way that we would tackle it using

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.180
the standard algorithm,
probably the way that your

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.990
parents first learned to multiply

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.910
multi-digit numbers like this

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.210
is we'll take all of the numbers in 6742,

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:05.560
all of the various places,
and multiply it by three.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.470
And then we're gonna
multiply it times two 10s.

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.190
And then we're gonna add everything up.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:11.730
So let's first multiply it times three.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.330
So we have two times three, that is six.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.950
Then we have four times three.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.047
And what people often say is,

00:01:18.047 --> 00:01:20.997
"Four times three is 12, write the two,

00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:22.850
"and then carry the one."

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.810
But what really just happened is you said

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:28.960
four 10s times three is 12 10s.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.960
12 10s can be written as two 10s plus 100.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.110
Then we say seven times three is 21.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.527
And then you'll say, "Oh, I
have to add that other one,

00:01:39.527 --> 00:01:41.167
"so I get 22."

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.250
But once again, what just happened?

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.217
We said seven hundreds times three is 2100

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.330
plus another hundred is 22 hundreds,

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:53.360
which can be expressed as two hundreds

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.930
and two thousands.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:59.290
And then, last but not
least, six times three is 18

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.560
plus two is 20.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.680
But remember, we're
talking about thousands.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.653
So this is 20 thousands.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:11.570
So then we will move on to
the two 10s right over here.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.150
So two times two 10s is four 10s.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.350
Now some folks might be tempted to put

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.500
the four over there,
but that's not four 10s.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.280
Four 10s would be right over here.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.110
And so it's common practice as you move

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:26.120
to the next place value
over, as you get to this two,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.670
that people will just put a zero here

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.830
just so they don't make that mistake.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.020
All right, now let's keep going.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.660
What is four times two?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:36.580
Well that's eight.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.130
We'll just write the
eight right over there.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:38.963
Why did that work?

00:02:38.963 --> 00:02:42.150
Well we're having four 10s times two 10s,

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:42.983
well that's going to be

00:02:42.983 --> 00:02:45.710
eight times 10 times 10, eight hundreds.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.950
And then we say what is seven times two.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.820
That is 14, which of course we can write

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:56.570
the four and then we can
carry the one, so to speak.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:58.660
And I'll cross these out
so I don't get confused.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.660
And then six times two is
going to be equal to 12,

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.990
plus this one that we had carried, is 13.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.010
So there we go.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:13.200
And then we just have
to add everything up.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.000
And we are going to get

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.430
six plus zero ones is six.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.060
Two 10s plus four 10s is six 10s.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.850
Two hundreds plus eight
hundreds is 10 hundreds,

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.510
which you could do as zero
hundreds and one thousand.

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.160
One thousand plus zero
thousands plus four thousands

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.170
is five thousands.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:36.660
Two 10 thousands plus three 10 thousands

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.820
is going to be five 10 thousands.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.230
And then we just have one hundred thousand

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.063
right over there.

00:03:43.063 --> 00:03:46.210
So we've got 155,066.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.743
And we are done.

